$\begin{align}
0.5^2 &= 0.5 \cdot 0.5
\\\\
&=0.25
\end{align}$

Since $0.5$ is five tenths, we can use fractions instead:

$\begin{align}
0.5^2 &= \dfrac{5}{10} \cdot \dfrac{5}{10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{5 \cdot 5}{10 \cdot 10}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{25}{100}
\\\\
&=0.25 &&\gray{\text{(Twenty-five hundredths)}}
\end{align}$
